    "question": {
      ":question/id": "4e96aa6b-3f6f-55a6-b340-4edb16b98dd2",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following elementary row operations transforms the matrix  $C$ into the matrix $D$, where \n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 7 & 2 \\\\ -6 & 1 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 7 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that the $2$nd row is the same in both matrices. The only rows that have changed are the $1$st and $3$rd rows.\n\nBy considering the given row operations that change both the $1$st and $3$rd rows, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 7 & 2 \\\\ -6 & 1 & 6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1}\u2194{R}_{3} \\\\ & \\sim\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 7 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ & =D.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}\u2194{R}_{3}.\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "c437d274-a3d9-5eff-8117-28c43670d91b",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "6c056370-b965-5440-bcea-d055e549b33a",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "623f2235-d2db-5966-b23b-44106c847d73",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "{R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {R}_{1}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "0a27db83-e5b8-5ced-a9b6-0e7ed682c1de",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "{R}_{1}\u2194{R}_{3}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "9f3e0784-d06f-5cb8-88dc-314a620963b7",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "{R}_{1}:=3\\cdot {R}_{1}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "3a0b953b-83f1-5d3c-9aff-0dd03d04ee29",
